    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Formed on 1 January 1801 by the union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a> and Ireland, with a single Parliament at Westminster.</li><li>The first industrial nation, it led world trade and finance and ruled the largest empire in history.</li><li>Irish grievances, deepened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-famine-ireland">Great Famine</a>, led to the Easter Rising, a war of independence and the Irish Free State in 1922.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Ireland’s population fell from about 8.2 million in 1841 to about 4.4 million in 1911 through famine deaths and emigration, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>’s more than doubled.</p></aside>
    </section>

